abstract:
*PCL guides tested in this study seem to be biocompatible: signs of&#13;
rejection were never detected. The presence of a new-formed bone witness&#13;
osteo-conductivity of the scaffold. Histological data showed that&#13;
osteogenesis mainly arise from the periostium of ulna, initially reacting&#13;
to form a bridge toward the scaffold. Further studies should investigate&#13;
if modifications in the composition of the scaffold may increase&#13;
its osteoconductivity and osteoinductivity.
